    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:Philip has 20 cows. He has 50% more ducks, so he has 20 * 0.50 = 10 more ducks. He has a total of 20 + 10 = 30 ducks. He also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. One-fifth of ducks and cows is 30/5 = 6 ducks and cows. So he has 6 ducks and cows. The total number of animals Philip has on his farm is 20 cows + 30 ducks + 6 pigs = 56 animals. #### 56 The answer is: 56

